Junkhaven Privacy Policy
Effective date: November 17, 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how Junkhaven ("the game," "we," "us") handles information when you play on your Android device. The game is developed by GOBLIN STEW.
The short version
Junkhaven does not collect, sell, or share your personal information. There are no accounts, no ads, and no analytics in the game. Your progress stays on your device.
Information we collect
We do not collect any personal information. Specifically, the game does not collect your name, email address, location, contacts, photos, microphone or camera data, or device identifiers.
Information stored on your device
The game saves your progress, settings, and game data locally on your device so you can pick up where you left off. This data is not sent to us or to any third party. Uninstalling the game removes this data.
Your device's own backup feature may also include the game's save data. If your Android backup is turned on, that backup is handled by Google and controlled through your device's settings. We do not have access to it.
Google Play Games cloud saves
Junkhaven may let you sync your progress using Google Play Games cloud saves. If you choose to sign in to Google Play Games, your save data is stored in your Google account and is handled by Google under Google's Privacy Policy. We do not receive, access, or store that data. Cloud saves are optional, and the game works without signing in.
Third-party services
Junkhaven does not include third-party advertising, analytics, or crash-reporting services. If you downloaded the game from Google Play, Google may collect information about your installation and use of Play according to Google's Privacy Policy. We do not control that collection.
Permissions
The game does not request any sensitive Android permissions.
Children's privacy
Because we do not collect personal information from anyone, we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you are a parent or guardian and have questions, contact us using the details below.
Changes to this policy
If the game changes in a way that affects your privacy (for example, adding ads or online features), we will update this policy and change the effective date above.
